# EXAMPLE / PLACEHOLDER — this file is not a key. Never commit a real key.
#
# Local dev: generate an ignored key once, then start the backend:
#   scripts/dev_gen_jwt_key.sh        # writes ops/identity/jwt_private_key.pem (gitignored)
#
# Production: do NOT use a repo file. Inject the key as a Docker/Kubernetes secret
# mounted read-only at /run/secrets/identity_jwt_private_key
# (see compose.prod.yaml and ops/identity/README.md).
#
# The real ops/identity/jwt_private_key.pem is a PEM RSA key: a "BEGIN/END" header
# pair wrapping base64 lines. It is generated locally and never pasted here.
